    ddx: ["Acute Surgical Pain", "Compartment Syndrome", "Wound Infection", "DVT"],
    goals: "Achieve adequate pain control (target pain score <4/10), facilitate early mobilisation, prevent chronic pain, minimise opioid use",
    pharm: "1. WHO Analgesic Ladder Step 2 (moderate pain not controlled by Step 1): Add Tramadol 50-100mg PO/IM q6h PRN (max 400mg/day). 2. Continue Paracetamol 1g QID (scheduled, not PRN). 3. Continue Diclofenac 75mg IM/PO BID (max 5-7 days, add PPI cover). 4. If pain still uncontrolled, escalate to WHO Step 3: Morphine 5-10mg PO/SC q4h PRN. 5. Neuropathic component: add Gabapentin 300mg at bedtime (or Pregabalin 75mg BID) if nerve injury suspected. 6. Laxative (Lactulose 15mL BID or Senna) if on opioids. 7. Antiemetic (Ondansetron 4mg TID PRN) for opioid nausea.",
    nonPharm: "Elevation of left leg. Ice packs to surgical site 20 mins on/off. Early physiotherapy for mobilisation. Relaxation techniques. Adequate sleep hygiene.",
