    chiefComplaint: "Chronic low back pain radiating to the right leg for 6 months, worse with sitting",
    hpi: "L.M., 19-year-old Tailor from Voi, presents with a 6-month history of chronic low back pain radiating to the right leg (sciatica distribution — buttock, posterior thigh, and lateral calf). The pain is burning and shooting in quality, rated 7/10, worse with sitting (especially on low chairs) and bending forward, partially relieved by lying down. Reports tingling and numbness along the right lateral shin and dorsum of the foot. No bowel or bladder dysfunction (no cauda equina). No bilateral symptoms. No fever, weight loss, or night pain. Previous treatment with ibuprofen and physiotherapy provided minimal relief.",
    pmh: "No significant PMH. Non-smoker. No history of cancer. No diabetes. Previous episode of low back pain 3 years ago (resolved with physiotherapy).. Also has Type 2 Diabetes.",
